<ParahumanWikiLayout>
  <div slot="title">The People's Power</div>
  <p>The People's Power is a villainous group founded on communist principles. Its members are known for stealing
  from the wealthy to support their large unpowered membership.</p>
  <div class="warning">Some members of this team have highly dangerous abilities that affect large areas. If you believe you're in
  the vicinity of this team during a cape fight, run away and create as much distance as possible.</div>

  <h2>Known Members</h2>
  <h3>Blindspot</h3>
  <p>Blindspot has pitch black skin and is highly athletic. She has only very rarely been spotted in public.
  Other powers are speculated, such as a possible danger sense, to account for the fact that she is rarely
  seen, even by authorities during a crime-in-progress.</p>
  <h3>Abyss</h3>
  <p>Abyss can create a bottomless pit around herself, which moves as she does. She wears a dark blue costume with light armouring.</p>
  <div class="helpExpand">
    Help us expand this section.
    <ul>
      <li>How does Abyss avoid falling into her own pit?</li>
      <li>What happens to matter that intersects with the empty space when she activates her power?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <h3>Uproot</h3>
  <p>Uproot wears a costume with a patchwork design.</p>
  <p>Uproot can teleport everything in a large area to seemingly any location. This ability
  causes massive property damage due to it affecting underground infrastructure and walls and ceilings of buildings.</p>
  <p>Uproot was also the subject of a highly controversial incident with BOPA. See <a href="/parahumans/bopa#incident">2024 BOPA Inhumane Interrogation Incident</a>.
  <h3>Zip</h3>
  <p>Zip appears to be a boy of around age 12 who dresses in a white costume with red stripes. His power is that
  he can dash short distances extremely quickly, with a very short cooldown.</p>
</ParahumanWikiLayout>